---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "./header.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <Header />

  <main class="methods-page">
    <div class="methods-content">
      <header class="page-intro">
        <h1>Methods</h1>
        <p>[Overview]</p>
      </header>

      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="method-1">
        <h2 id="method-1">Data</h2>

        <div class="method-row">
          <div class="method-main">
            <h3>Population</h3>
            <p>
              Information on patients diagnosed with primary malignant HNC
              cancer in England from 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2021 from
              National Cancer Registration Dataset (NCRD)<sup
                ><a href="#ref-1" aria-label="1">1</a></sup
              > and from 1 January 2022 - 31 December 2023 from the Rapid Cancer Registration
              Database (RCRD).
            </p>
            <h3>Access</h3>
            <p>
              The NHS England Secure Data Environment (SDE) was used to access
              the cancer data. In line with the SDE disclosure policy, counts
              are rounded to the nearest five and those below 10 are suppressed.
              Analyses were carried out in STATA version 18.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="method-extra" aria-label="Additional information">
            <h3>[Definition or additional detail]</h3>
            <p>[Placeholder]</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="method-2">
        <h2 id="method-2">Approach</h2>

        <div class="method-row">
          <div class="method-main">
            <h3>Incidence</h3>
            <p>
              Incidence rates per 100,000 person-years were derived using Office
              for National Statistics (ONS) mid-year population estimates for
              the years 2016-2022 by age, sex and Lower-level Super Output Area
              (LSOA). Incidence for 2023 was derived using 2022 population
              denominators.
            </p>
            <h3>Survival</h3>
            <p>
              Estimates of one- and five-year net survival estimates were
              derived using the most up-to-date methodology.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="method-extra" aria-label="Additional information">
            <h3>[Definition or additional detail]</h3>
            <p>[Placeholder]</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="method-3">
        <h2 id="method-3">Covariables</h2>

        <div class="method-row">
          <div class="method-main">
            <h3>Deprivation</h3>
            <p>
              Patients' deprivation was classified according to quintiles of
              Index of Multiple Deprivation 2019 at LSOA level.
            </p>
            <h3>Region</h3>
            <p>Government Office Region of residence at cancer diagnosis.</p>
            <h3>Stage</h3>
            <p>
              Information on how advanced the cancer was at diagnosis was
              recorded in the NCRD for diagnoses up to 2021. Stage was
              unavailable for 2022-2023. Tumours were grouped into early (TNM I
              and II), advanced (III and IV), or unknown.
            </p>
            <h3>Route to diagnosis</h3>
            <p>
              The pathway taken by patients through the health service to cancer
              diagnosis was available for NCRD data up to 2018. The Rapid Cancer
              Registration Database (RCRD) includes unvalidated estimates for
              2022-2023. Patient pathways were categorised into Emergency or
              Non-Emergency routes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="img-extra" aria-label="Additional information">
            <img
              src="/HNCancer/images/English_regions.svg.png"
              style="width: 100%; max-width: 500px;"
              alt="Map showing the nine English regions"
            />
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="references" aria-labelledby="references-title">
        <h2 id="references-title">References</h2>
        <ol>
          <li id="ref-1">
            Henson KE, Elliss-Brookes L, Coupland VH, et al. Data Resource
            Profile: National Cancer Registration Dataset in England.
            International Journal of Epidemiology 2019;49(1):16-16h. doi:
            <a href="https://academic.oup.com/ije/article/49/1/16/5476570"
              >10.1093/ije/dyz076</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>[Author or organisation. (Year). Title of source.]</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .methods-page {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem) 1.25rem;
  }

  .methods-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .methods-content > * + * {
    margin-block-start: 3rem;
  }

  .page-intro > * + *,
  .method-section > * + *,
  .method-main > * + *,
  .method-extra > * + *,
  .img-extra > * + * {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }

  .method-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .method-main {
    flex: 2 1 30rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .method-extra,
  .img-extra {
    flex: 1 1 14rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .method-extra {
    background: var(--bulma-background);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--bulma-border);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .references {
    padding-block-start: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bulma-border);
  }

  .references > * + * {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }

  .references ol {
    padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .references li + li {
    margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
  }

  .method-main sup {
    font-size: 0.75em;
    vertical-align: super;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .method-main sup a {
    text-decoration: none;
    padding-inline: 0.1em;
  }

  .method-main sup a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  img {
    display: block;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .methods-page {
      padding-inline: 1rem;
    }

    .method-row {
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
